[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n3_godric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Abbot Godric at dusk, in the chapter house (night 3). Small, frail, very old and kind; he leans on his crosier and coughs.
# Not in the cult. Drugged hardest, he believes the demon has come, and has ordered more incense to drive it out.
== start
(The abbot sits alone on the stone bench, both hands on his crosier. The air in here is blue with incense.)
Abbot Godric: Come in, my son. Let an old man look at you. You've lost colour since you came to us.
-> topics

== again
(The abbot coughs into his sleeve for a long while before he can speak.)
Abbot Godric: Forgive me. The smoke. A small price for the safety of the house.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n3_godric_demon] Is there truly a demon in the house, Father Abbot? -> demon
* [if not n3_godric_porter] How am I doing as porter, Father Abbot? -> porter
* [if not n3_godric_blessing] Will you bless me, Father Abbot? -> blessing

== demon [set n3_godric_demon]
Abbot Godric: It has come into our house. I said so before the brothers this morning, and I'll say it again.
Abbot Godric: I have felt it at the night office, my son. The way you feel a draught from a door left open.
Abbot Godric: So we'll smoke it out. Incense at every office, and prayer. Our saint will not suffer it long.
-> topics

== porter [set n3_godric_porter]
Abbot Godric: Thomas tells me you keep good hours, and you ring the bell well. That's most of it.
Abbot Godric: The prior is harder to please. He's no harder on you than he is on himself. Bear with him.
Abbot Godric: Anselm kept that gate thirty years. Be patient with yourself. It took him a while too.
-> topics

== blessing [set n3_godric_blessing]
(You kneel. His hand on your head is as light as paper, and it shakes.)
Abbot Godric: The Lord bless you and keep you, and keep the gate through you. Go in peace, my son.
(He signs the cross over you, and coughs.)
-> topics
"
